   "text": "# Code review: `interface/forms/eye_mag/report.php`\n\n## Critical / High: security\n\n**1. SQL injection in `display_draw_image()`**\n- `$sql = \"SELECT * from documents where documents.url like '%\".$filename.\"'\";`\n- `$filename` is built from `$pid` and `$encounter`.\n- At the top of the file those can be overwritten straight from `$_REQUEST['ptid']` and `$_REQUEST['encid']`. The value reaches the query unsanitized.\n- **Fix:** use a bound parameter.\n- **Severity: Critical**\n\n**2. Cross-patient document disclosure via LIKE matching (same query)**\n- The pattern has a leading `%`, and `_` is a LIKE wildcard.\n- So `'%1_123_OU_EXT_VIEW.jpg'` also matches `11_123_\u2026`, `21_123_\u2026`, `1x123\u2026`, and so on.\n- Patient A's report can therefore render patient B's drawings.\n- **Fix:** match on exact URL or `foreign_id`, filter by `pid`, and escape wildcards.\n- **Severity: High (PHI leak)**\n\n**3. Unauthenticated override of patient/encounter context, with no ACL check**\n- `$pid`, `$encounter`, `$form_id` and `$form_name` are taken from `$_REQUEST` (`ptid`, `encid`, `formid`, `formname`).\n- There is no `acl_check()` anywhere in the file.\n- Any logged-in user can render any patient's full exam by changing the URL (IDOR).\n- **Severity: High**\n\n**4. Stored XSS: many DB fields echoed without `text()`/`attr()`**\n- `$HPI1` (the other HPIs are escaped).\n- `$CHRONIC2`, `$CHRONIC3`.\n- `$CTLOSVA`.\n- All motility values `$MOTILITY_*`.\n- In the IMPPLAN block:\n  - `$item['codetext']`, `$item['code']`, `$item['plan']`. The plan is `str_replace`d to `<br />` and printed raw; it should be escaped first, then newlines converted.\n  - `$PLAN` items and `$PLAN2`.\n- `$note->get_note()` in `display_draw_image()`.\n- `$providerNAME` in the PDF signature line.\n- `$from_file` / `$filetoshow` in `<img src>`. These include `$pid` from `$_REQUEST`, which also makes them reflected XSS.\n- `$form_folder` in the Amsler `<img src>`.\n- **Severity: High**\n\n**5. String-concatenated SQL**\n- `\"select * from facility where id=\" . $_SESSION['pc_facility']`\n- The value comes from the session, but this should still be parameterized.\n- **Severity: Medium**\n\n**6. `@extract($objQuery)` / `@extract($encounter_data)`**\n- These dump every column of `form_encounter.*` and `form_eye_mag.*` into local scope, with errors suppressed.\n- Columns such as `pid`, `encounter`, `id`, `provider_id`, `form_id` silently overwrite function parameters and locals. Any future column whose name collides with a local variable (e.g. `choice`, `cols`) will change behaviour.\n- **Fix:** access the result array explicitly.\n- **Severity: Medium**\n\n**7. `$$LOCATION = text($prefs['GOVALUE']);` at global scope**\n- These are DB-driven variable variables. They can clobber any global, including `$pid`, `$encounter` and `$GLOBALS` config.\n- They are also HTML-escaped at assignment, which risks double-escaping later.\n- **Severity: Medium**\n\n## High: correctness\n\n**8. `$choice` is never set**\n- `if ($_REQUEST['CHOICE']) $choice = $_REQUEST['choice'];` checks `CHOICE` but reads `choice`. The key case is inconsistent.\n\n**9. Choice dispatch logic is inverted**\n- `else if ($choice != \"narrative\")` means `choice=narrative` renders nothing.\n- The doc block says narrative/absent should display everything.\n- It also documents `NARRATIVE` (uppercase) while comparing lowercase.\n\n**10. Short open tags `<?`**\n- They appear after the `CC2` block and in the commented DRAW code.\n- With `short_open_tag=Off`, the `<?` is emitted as literal text. The `}` inside it is no longer PHP, so the brace structure breaks and the file fails to parse.\n\n**11. `$$zone[$i]` in the motility loop**\n- PHP 7 parses this as `($$zone)[$i]`, not `${$zone[$i]}`.\n- On PHP 7+ the motility values are never transformed. It may also raise array-to-string notices.\n- **Fix:** use `${$zone[$i]}`.\n\n**12. Wrong motility cell**\n- The left-eye bottom row prints `$MOTILITY_LLIO` twice.\n- The first cell should be `$MOTILITY_LRIO`.\n- This is clinically incorrect output.\n\n**13. Queries don't filter `forms.formdir` and ignore the form id**\n- Both encounter queries join `form_eye_mag.id = forms.form_id` without `forms.formdir='eye_mag'`. They can match another form type's row that happens to share the id.\n- The first query (`eye_mag_report`) also lacks `forms.deleted` filtering.\n- Neither query uses `$id`/`$form_id`, so with multiple eye_mag forms in one encounter an arbitrary one is shown.\n\n**14. Typos in conditions that hide data**\n| Location | Condition as written | Should be |\n|---|---|---|\n| ccNear row | `$ODNEARVA_1\\|\\|$WNEAROSVA_1` | `$OSNEARVA_1` |\n| Gonioscopy | `$ODGONIO\\|\\|$OSDGONIO` | `$OSGONIO` |\n| Additional data | `$PAMODBA` | `$PAMODVA` |\n| NPC | `$ODNPC or $OSNPC` (then prints `$NPC`) | `$NPC` |\n\n- Retina guard: `$ODDISC||$OSDISC||$ODCUP||$ODMACULA||$ODVESSELS||$ODPERIPH` omits the OS fields. Left-eye-only cup, macula, vessel or periphery findings are not reported.\n- Refraction guard uses `$ODVA||$OSVA`, but the wearing Rx values live in `$ODVA_1` etc. Current glasses may not display.\n\n**15. AR comments block uses the stale loop variable**\n- It reads `${\"COMMENTS_$i\"}` after the Rx loop, where `$i == $count_rx+1`. The value is undefined or wrong.\n- The \"Comments:\" label there is also untranslated.\n\n**16. Character replacement corrupts UTF-8 in IMPPLAN `plan`**\n- `\"\\x85\"` replaces a single byte that occurs as a UTF-8 continuation byte (e.g. `\u2026`, `\u00c5`). This corrupts multibyte text.\n- `\"\\u2028\"` / `\"\\u2029\"` are not escapes in PHP (PHP 7 needs `\\u{2028}`), so they match the literal text \"\\u2028\".\n\n**17. Signature date is misleading**\n- \"electronically signed on\" uses `oeFormatShortDate()`, which is today's date at render time, not the actual signing date.\n- This is a medico-legal concern.\n- **Severity: High (clinical record)**\n\n## Medium: reliability and HTML\n\n**18. Uninitialized variables**\n- `$IMPPLAN_items`: `foreach` warns when there are no rows.\n- `$bad`.\n- `$display_Add`.\n- `$css_header`: not declared `global` in `narrative()`, so the stylesheet href is empty.\n\n**19. Empty encounter date silently shows today**\n- `new DateTime($encounter_date)` with a null or empty value yields the current date.\n- If the query returns no row, the report shows today as the visit date.\n\n**20. Malformed HTML**\n- Pupils `<td>`: opened when `$PUPIL_NORMAL=='1'`, but `</td>` is only emitted inside the `$ODPUPILSIZE1||$OSPUPILSIZE1` branch.\n- ACT table: `</tr><tr>` is emitted only inside `if ($ACT5CCDIST)`.\n- `<table style=\"report_vitals\" style=\"...\">` has a duplicate `style` attribute.\n- Refraction header has 10 columns while the title uses `colspan=\"9\"`.\n\n**21. `$document_id > '1'` excludes document id 1**\n- The comparison is also string-vs-int.\n\n**22. Missing `echo` loses the tooltip**\n- `<?php xla('Variation in red...'); ?>` has no `echo`, so the title attribute is empty.\n\n## Low: maintainability and i18n\n\n**23. Dead code and debug leftovers**\n- `left_overs()` references undefined variables.\n- `full_report()` returns immediately and contains a duplicated `print(\"<tr>\\n\")`.\n- The large commented-out DRAW block.\n- Unused `$titleres`, `$facility`, `$visit_date`, `$extension`, `$to_file`.\n- `xlt('Type').$count_rx` prints the Rx count in the column header.\n- Cache-buster parameter named `blahblah`.\n\n**24. Translation strings**\n- Malformed: `xlt('sc Near{{without correction near')` is missing the closing `}}`.\n- Typos: \"Constaast\", \"Cyinder\", \"Accomodation\".\n- Untranslated: \"Orders/Next Visit:\", \"Full to CF OU\", \"Comments:\".\n\n**25. Inconsistent globals and paths**\n- Mixes `$GLOBALS['web_root']`, `$GLOBALS['webroot']` and `global $web_root`.\n- `eom.bmp` vs `eom.jpg`.\n- The `<img heght=75>` typo appears in commented code.\n\n**26. Massive copy/paste**\n- The HPI \u00d73, refraction rows and ACT grids \u00d74 should be helper functions or loops.\n- The near-identical document-path code appears twice.\n\n**27. File ending**\n- Trailing `?>` with no final newline; omit the closing tag to avoid stray output.\n\n**Recommendation:** do not merge until 1\u20134, 8\u201314, and 17 are fixed."
